"""Exact production C1 target on real anchors (DIAGNOSTIC_NOT_CLAIM).

The checked-in pilot source rows carry a *surrogate* C1/C2 label
(`PILOT_PRIMITIVE_SOURCE_FALLBACK = True`, scripts/run_v025_pilot_c3.py:89),
so they cannot be used to characterise the production target defined at
src/mcrl/physics_v025/targets.py:154 (`c1_difference_surplus`).

This probe rebuilds a handful of real anchors on the same tape/setting the
pilot used, evaluates every shortlisted *unilateral* configuration through the
sealed engine's coupled-power boundary, and records the exact production C1
label together with its per-user-bits decomposition:

    y(u,a) = [ (B_a - B_0) - eta (E_a - E_0) ] / kappa + (phi_a - phi_0)
           = own(u,a) + ext(u,a) + energy(u,a) + phi(u,a)

    own = ( b_u(a) - b_u(0) ) / kappa                 focal user's own bits
    ext = sum_{j != u} ( b_j(a) - b_j(0) ) / kappa    whole-network externality
    energy = -eta ( E_a - E_0 ) / kappa
    phi = Phi(a) - Phi(0)                             closed form, pre-decision

The 16-D Q1 feature vector produced for the same (anchor, user, action) is
stored alongside so that level-vs-order questions can be asked with the
admissible feature set.

No training, no policy run, no constant/threshold/seed/horizon change; nothing
under /home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover is touched and no sealed artefact is written.

    PYTHONPATH=src nice -n 15 /home/sat/mcrl-leo-handover/.venv/bin/python \
        scripts/probe_c1_production_target.py --anchors 6
